{"reference":"Ezekiel 26","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":26,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading Tyre in Ezekiel 26–28","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Ezekiel 26 begins a sequence addressing historical Tyre and its rulers. The later chapters develop related images of ships, lament, a garden, precious stones, and a cherub; the sequence does not explicitly name Satan. Therefore, reading these chapters as a direct description of Satan is a disputed interpretation rather than an explicit identification in the text.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 26:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_026_ec31103c6461e7f68a33127f"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}